(3411869, 475016, 63503, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture. The climber is placed following the rule of thirds, so, nobody could fault you for that. I also like your keeping the climber little, thereby giving the much needed sense of great height; however, I am not sure that the rule  of thirds powewr point is the best placement for the climber in this case. I imagine you did try other crops and ended up with this (9)</td>', 'Beautiful picture. The climber is placed following the rule of thirds, so, nobody could fault you for that. I also like your keeping the climber little, thereby giving the much needed sense of great height; however, I am not sure that the rule  of thirds powewr point is the best placement for the climber in this case. I imagine you did try other crops and ended up with this (9)', '2007-02-28 00:58:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411870, 476411, 63503, '<td valign="top">beautiful image.</td>', 'beautiful image.', '2007-02-28 00:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411887, 476874, 63503, '<td valign="top">Great Image!!! I hope that was an already broken watch. Beautiful lighting, focus and DOF (10)</td>', 'Great Image!!! I hope that was an already broken watch. Beautiful lighting, focus and DOF (10)', '2007-02-28 01:03:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411896, 475867, 73451, '<td valign="top">Very nice</td>', 'Very nice', '2007-02-28 01:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411903, 476398, 73451, '<td valign="top">Nice curve of the body. Not sure if I like the piece of ice.  Might have used a bigger piece.</td>', 'Nice curve of the body. Not sure if I like the piece of ice.  Might have used a bigger piece.', '2007-02-28 01:07:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411925, 476313, 36065, '<td valign="top">I like this type of shot a lot, as the lighting potential with these is endless.  You produced some terrific color here, but the hot spot on the center of the ice is too strong.  It grabs my eye and just holds it there.  I did a similar shot, and I''ll give you a not so secretive secret.  Light it from the bottom.  I punched a hole in a black cloth, put in on some glass, set the ice of the hole and put the flash under the table.  The ice lit much more evenly, and without so much of a hot spot.  Great start, and nice job meeting the challenge.</td>', 'I like this type of shot a lot, as the lighting potential with these is endless.  You produced some terrific color here, but the hot spot on the center of the ice is too strong.  It grabs my eye and just holds it there.  I did a similar shot, and I''ll give you a not so secretive secret.  Light it from the bottom.  I punched a hole in a black cloth, put in on some glass, set the ice of the hole and put the flash under the table.  The ice lit much more evenly, and without so much of a hot spot.  Great start, and nice job meeting the challenge.', '2007-02-28 01:13:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411926, 474316, 70103, '<td valign="top">The house in the background seems to be a distraction. This could be stronger if you concentrated on the ice</td>', 'The house in the background seems to be a distraction. This could be stronger if you concentrated on the ice', '2007-02-28 01:14:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411928, 474271, 70103, '<td valign="top">It''s a little too dark but a nice photo</td>', 'It''s a little too dark but a nice photo', '2007-02-28 01:15:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411933, 473133, 36065, '<td valign="top">I see a lot of noise in this one.  It looks like is was taken with a pretty high ISO, so backing that down a bit and increasing you exposure time would have helped that out.  Or, using a bit of Neat Image will also pull out the noise.  I do like the feel of speed and movement that you created, but the tree limb is a bit distracting.  A different point of view would have helped out some as well.</td>', 'I see a lot of noise in this one.  It looks like is was taken with a pretty high ISO, so backing that down a bit and increasing you exposure time would have helped that out.  Or, using a bit of Neat Image will also pull out the noise.  I do like the feel of speed and movement that you created, but the tree limb is a bit distracting.  A different point of view would have helped out some as well.', '2007-02-28 01:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411945, 476589, 67237, '<td valign="top">creative!</td>', 'creative!', '2007-02-28 01:18:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411951, 472809, 36065, '<td valign="top">I do notice the ice as soon as I look at your image, but I don''t think that your ice is as large of an element as it needed to be.  I will not say that you didn''t meet the challenge, but I think you just squeezed it in there.</td>', 'I do notice the ice as soon as I look at your image, but I don''t think that your ice is as large of an element as it needed to be.  I will not say that you didn''t meet the challenge, but I think you just squeezed it in there.', '2007-02-28 01:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411961, 476560, 70103, '<td valign="top">it''s a nice photo but too small, save it at least with 640 pixels on one side next time</td>', 'it''s a nice photo but too small, save it at least with 640 pixels on one side next time', '2007-02-28 01:25:48.000000', NULL, 1),
