(3420907, 474369, 62637, '<td valign="top">Interesting take on this one.  I see you''ve gone for the mysterious "nothing is in focus" effect,  I really get a sense for the chaos of an intense winter storm.  I also really enjoy the "revenge of the motorist" motif you''ve applied here; by reducing the cyclist to lowly pedestrianism, you illustrate the superiority of the automobile.  You know, the lack of detail and motion blurring gives this a very painting like quality that I find lacking in so many photographs today.  A stroke of pure genius, 10.</td>', 'Interesting take on this one.  I see you''ve gone for the mysterious "nothing is in focus" effect,  I really get a sense for the chaos of an intense winter storm.  I also really enjoy the "revenge of the motorist" motif you''ve applied here; by reducing the cyclist to lowly pedestrianism, you illustrate the superiority of the automobile.  You know, the lack of detail and motion blurring gives this a very painting like quality that I find lacking in so many photographs today.  A stroke of pure genius, 10.', '2007-03-01 21:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
