(3435666, 476790, 67697, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this did not score higher.  It is a good pic.  And except for one, you got some really good comments there.  For something like this where you are playing with the lighting, try adding a solid background and see what happens.  should be an interesting effect.  I didn''t get to vote on this but i would have given this a 7!</td>', 'I''m surprised this did not score higher.  It is a good pic.  And except for one, you got some really good comments there.  For something like this where you are playing with the lighting, try adding a solid background and see what happens.  should be an interesting effect.  I didn''t get to vote on this but i would have given this a 7!', '2007-03-07 00:21:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3435712, 473102, 50641, '<td valign="top">Ack, I''m sorry I didn''t comment on this during the challenge. I liked it!  I gave it a 7.  I don''t understand how it wound up with a 5.28.  The subject is unmistakeable and so fitting and the shot has that gorgeous depth and sky.  And it makes me feel like going out to the Delaware to see what''s going on :)  P.S. I see the shade was criticized.  I think it''s a natural-looking photo, which has merit. Sometimes I use the flash (as fill) or a flashlight to paint in shady cases like this. Doesn''t always work out.</td>', 'Ack, I''m sorry I didn''t comment on this during the challenge. I liked it!  I gave it a 7.  I don''t understand how it wound up with a 5.28.  The subject is unmistakeable and so fitting and the shot has that gorgeous depth and sky.  And it makes me feel like going out to the Delaware to see what''s going on :)  P.S. I see the shade was criticized.  I think it''s a natural-looking photo, which has merit. Sometimes I use the flash (as fill) or a flashlight to paint in shady cases like this. Doesn''t always work out.', '2007-03-07 00:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
