(3438304, 476122, 30861, '<td valign="top">haha! He''s alive and well, David.</td>', 'haha! He''s alive and well, David.', '2007-03-07 13:14:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438335, 474369, 30861, '<td valign="top">I have a hard time believing this scored THAT bad. IN many ways, it''s the frigid essence of ice-as-we-experience-it in our daily lives, and I gave you a 7 for this one. Just wanted you to know someone actually appreciated it :-)</td>', 'I have a hard time believing this scored THAT bad. IN many ways, it''s the frigid essence of ice-as-we-experience-it in our daily lives, and I gave you a 7 for this one. Just wanted you to know someone actually appreciated it :-)', '2007-03-07 13:20:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438368, 474369, 35545, '<td valign="top">Darn.  I didn''t vote on the challenge, but I really think you were robbed.  This is a beautiful shot -- should have scored much higher.</td>', 'Darn.  I didn''t vote on the challenge, but I really think you were robbed.  This is a beautiful shot -- should have scored much higher.', '2007-03-07 13:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438444, 476398, 33672, '<td valign="top">What a great photo! I think you achieved exactly what you were trying for. Great shadows, professional comp, nice detail and an incredible concept! Congrats on your PB and a top twenty finish!</td>', 'What a great photo! I think you achieved exactly what you were trying for. Great shadows, professional comp, nice detail and an incredible concept! Congrats on your PB and a top twenty finish!', '2007-03-07 13:40:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438451, 475983, 46663, '<td valign="top">Craig, I think you framed this picture well, although I am not so sure about the border.  I hesitate to say anything about the border, as I enjoy experiementing with borders too.  Your border doesn''t detract from the shot at all, but I am wondering if that affected some of the score.  I didn''t vote in this challenge, as there is little ice to be found in Arizona, but I think you captured the challenge well.  I am sure it is difficult to capture snow and ice (which is sooooo white) without causing it to look overexposed.  The photo made me shiver - which I think was your intent.  It looks so cold.  Thanks for sharing.</td>', 'Craig, I think you framed this picture well, although I am not so sure about the border.  I hesitate to say anything about the border, as I enjoy experiementing with borders too.  Your border doesn''t detract from the shot at all, but I am wondering if that affected some of the score.  I didn''t vote in this challenge, as there is little ice to be found in Arizona, but I think you captured the challenge well.  I am sure it is difficult to capture snow and ice (which is sooooo white) without causing it to look overexposed.  The photo made me shiver - which I think was your intent.  It looks so cold.  Thanks for sharing.', '2007-03-07 13:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438452, 476398, 53278, '<td valign="top">first let me start saying congrats on your high placement and on your average. as for this shot there is nothing really to comment on, everything was done superbly, lighting, composition etc...<br/> <br/>one thing thought if you somehow emphasize the light on the ice cube, and the water dripping around it, i think this would have scored higher.<br/> <br/>i think you can do that with selective color, chose white or neutral , absolute and drag the black bar all the way up(maybe).<br/> <br/>anyhow, great shot :)</td>', 'first let me start saying congrats on your high placement and on your average. as for this shot there is nothing really to comment on, everything was done superbly, lighting, composition etc... one thing thought if you somehow emphasize the light on the ice cube, and the water dripping around it, i think this would have scored higher. i think you can do that with selective color, chose white or neutral , absolute and drag the black bar all the way up(maybe). anyhow, great shot :)', '2007-03-07 13:41:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438514, 476773, 39057, '<td valign="top">Lowered the score b/c the table looked curved?<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lesgainous:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent capture. However, something odd stands out to the point where I can''t vote a little higher. The issue is that the table''s edge is not horizontal. It actually looks curved. Is the table (or whatever surface) not level? Or is there some lens aberration happening? </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Lowered the score b/c the table looked curved? Originally posted by lesgainous: Excellent capture. However, something odd stands out to the point where I can''t vote a little higher. The issue is that the table''s edge is not horizontal. It actually looks curved. Is the table (or whatever surface) not level? Or is there some lens aberration happening? ', '2007-03-07 13:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438551, 476398, 46202, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by zaflabout:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>one thing thought if you somehow emphasize the light on the ice cube, and the water dripping around it, i think this would have scored higher.<br/> <br/>i think you can do that with selective color, chose white or neutral , absolute and drag the black bar all the way up(maybe).</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, Hassan.  :o)  I agree with that completely, but due to the basic editing rules, I was unable to do so.  :oP  I may play around with it some now that the challenge is over, though.</td>', 'Originally posted by zaflabout: one thing thought if you somehow emphasize the light on the ice cube, and the water dripping around it, i think this would have scored higher. i think you can do that with selective color, chose white or neutral , absolute and drag the black bar all the way up(maybe).  Thanks, Hassan.  :o)  I agree with that completely, but due to the basic editing rules, I was unable to do so.  :oP  I may play around with it some now that the challenge is over, though.', '2007-03-07 13:52:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438556, 474057, 23484, '<td valign="top">Super shot Mary. You got robbed. The ice, water, and the tree reflections all flow together so nicely. I think this should have been top 10.</td>', 'Super shot Mary. You got robbed. The ice, water, and the tree reflections all flow together so nicely. I think this should have been top 10.', '2007-03-07 13:53:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438576, 475551, 65886, '<td valign="top">:)<br/>and it''s a huge compliment for me, too:) very cool image, your expression is excellent! really, and I also love it because it''s not a stereotypic ice queen, it'' ice but some weird emotions, too.</td>', ':)and it''s a huge compliment for me, too:) very cool image, your expression is excellent! really, and I also love it because it''s not a stereotypic ice queen, it'' ice but some weird emotions, too.', '2007-03-07 13:55:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438578, 476288, 23484, '<td valign="top">Alright, time for a refreshing dip in the pool. A little darker and you could have used this in low key. Great contrast.</td>', 'Alright, time for a refreshing dip in the pool. A little darker and you could have used this in low key. Great contrast.', '2007-03-07 13:56:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438605, 476773, 42013, '<td valign="top">Very Clean shot. Congrats on your ribbon.</td>', 'Very Clean shot. Congrats on your ribbon.', '2007-03-07 14:00:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438611, 475628, 26633, '<td valign="top">Interesting voting. I gave it a 10. I could stare at those lights for hours!</td>', 'Interesting voting. I gave it a 10. I could stare at those lights for hours!', '2007-03-07 14:01:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438614, 474234, 42013, '<td valign="top">Just a surreal image. Congrats!</td>', 'Just a surreal image. Congrats!', '2007-03-07 14:01:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438668, 476656, 52521, '<td valign="top">Congratulation on the blue! I love the out-take btw. ;)</td>', 'Congratulation on the blue! I love the out-take btw. ;)', '2007-03-07 14:12:37.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3438701, 475983, 30982, '<td valign="top">In my opinion, this does meet the challenge and you''ve got very good color in the water.  The composition is good with the diagonal of the water, but the picture overall lacks a bit in a point of interest.</td>', 'In my opinion, this does meet the challenge and you''ve got very good color in the water.  The composition is good with the diagonal of the water, but the picture overall lacks a bit in a point of interest.', '2007-03-07 14:19:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3438731, 475983, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals:  The image is soft.  This is probably a product of not being able to use USM as normal because of all the little twigs and such.  The exposure is on, but tough with all the snow.  I''d like to see a bit more texture there if there was any.<br/> <br/>The feel: the right side of the picture is just sorta blah.  I don''t like detrius like that at all.  But, whatcha going to do in the winter?  I do like the sloping curve of the river and the contrast of the whites and blues.<br/> <br/>The game: I think the stuff on the right hurt you and adds to a bit of a "snapshot" feel to it.  Working to see if you can have a similar image with something more appealing on the right would have been the challenge.</td>', 'The technicals:  The image is soft.  This is probably a product of not being able to use USM as normal because of all the little twigs and such.  The exposure is on, but tough with all the snow.  I''d like to see a bit more texture there if there was any. The feel: the right side of the picture is just sorta blah.  I don''t like detrius like that at all.  But, whatcha going to do in the winter?  I do like the sloping curve of the river and the contrast of the whites and blues. The game: I think the stuff on the right hurt you and adds to a bit of a "snapshot" feel to it.  Working to see if you can have a similar image with something more appealing on the right would have been the challenge.', '2007-03-07 14:25:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439129, 475983, 56828, '<td valign="top">I think you grabbed your colors very well. I think the location of the water in the upper left is what kept you under a 5.5.  That and the whole is snow and ice the same thing? (snow is ice).</td>', 'I think you grabbed your colors very well. I think the location of the water in the upper left is what kept you under a 5.5.  That and the whole is snow and ice the same thing? (snow is ice).', '2007-03-07 15:58:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439226, 476500, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the reflections and the clarity of the little flowers.  Nicely done</td>', 'I like the reflections and the clarity of the little flowers.  Nicely done', '2007-03-07 16:19:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439257, 476589, 811, '<td valign="top">Oh where oh where has the sense of humor gone, people.  This is hilarious.  AND it is technically well done.  Good work.  I think you were robbed.</td>', 'Oh where oh where has the sense of humor gone, people.  This is hilarious.  AND it is technically well done.  Good work.  I think you were robbed.', '2007-03-07 16:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439259, 476656, 54431, '<td valign="top">Wow...this is amazing. Beautiful shot! I would love to go to Iceland one day. Congrats on your ribbon, nice work!</td>', 'Wow...this is amazing. Beautiful shot! I would love to go to Iceland one day. Congrats on your ribbon, nice work!', '2007-03-07 16:25:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439260, 476484, 811, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and I like the shallow dof.  I am assuming those are thin pieces of ice?</td>', 'Nice colors and I like the shallow dof.  I am assuming those are thin pieces of ice?', '2007-03-07 16:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439305, 475551, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hey, this is TERRIFIC!</td>', 'Hey, this is TERRIFIC!', '2007-03-07 16:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439336, 476557, 7810, '<td valign="top">A very respectable finish for your first outing.<br/>Maybe you can merge a flame into the fireplace in the advanced edit :D<br/> <br/>Cheers!</td>', 'A very respectable finish for your first outing.Maybe you can merge a flame into the fireplace in the advanced edit :D Cheers!', '2007-03-07 16:36:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439538, 476398, 36065, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites in this challenge.  I like what you accomplished with low key here, and it is good to see that someone has a grasp of that technique.  Beyond that, your placement of the curves inside the frame give this one a terrific composition that grabs the eye and leads it through the frame, almost as if hands were massaging.  The placement of the ice near the center of the frame also gives the eye a nice focal point and leaves no doubt that the spirit of the challenge was indeed met.  Congrats on your highest score to date.  This one was well-deserved and I am sure that there are higher ones to come.  I like your take on the human form and the way you present and offer that to the rest of us.  To grow the vote, I think I might have left a little more negative space at the top of the frame.  While the composition is suiting, I think a more traditionally sized image may have done a bit better.  Nice work.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites in this challenge.  I like what you accomplished with low key here, and it is good to see that someone has a grasp of that technique.  Beyond that, your placement of the curves inside the frame give this one a terrific composition that grabs the eye and leads it through the frame, almost as if hands were massaging.  The placement of the ice near the center of the frame also gives the eye a nice focal point and leaves no doubt that the spirit of the challenge was indeed met.  Congrats on your highest score to date.  This one was well-deserved and I am sure that there are higher ones to come.  I like your take on the human form and the way you present and offer that to the rest of us.  To grow the vote, I think I might have left a little more negative space at the top of the frame.  While the composition is suiting, I think a more traditionally sized image may have done a bit better.  Nice work.', '2007-03-07 17:07:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439673, 476773, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Now if you stop using yellow/orange you might win a ribbon other than yellow. :P</td>', 'Congrats! Now if you stop using yellow/orange you might win a ribbon other than yellow. :P', '2007-03-07 17:42:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439716, 476656, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your Blue and a Stunning image!!</td>', 'Congratulations on your Blue and a Stunning image!!', '2007-03-07 17:50:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439728, 474234, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Ribbon!! Awesome image!!</td>', 'Congratulations on the Ribbon!! Awesome image!!', '2007-03-07 17:52:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439732, 476773, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Ribbon! VERY cool shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on the Ribbon! VERY cool shot!', '2007-03-07 17:53:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439740, 473376, 20941, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot! Congrats on a top ten!</td>', 'Awesome shot! Congrats on a top ten!', '2007-03-07 17:54:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439747, 475110, 20941, '<td valign="top">Stunning work! Congrats on a top ten!</td>', 'Stunning work! Congrats on a top ten!', '2007-03-07 17:55:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439752, 475618, 20941, '<td valign="top">Awesome Shot!! Congrats on a top ten!</td>', 'Awesome Shot!! Congrats on a top ten!', '2007-03-07 17:56:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439764, 475551, 20941, '<td valign="top">Great set up, fantastic work!! Congrats on the high placing and a Very Cool image!</td>', 'Great set up, fantastic work!! Congrats on the high placing and a Very Cool image!', '2007-03-07 17:58:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439814, 476845, 41337, '<td valign="top">If you''re struggling with this then it must be very difficult to shoot. Nice result.</td>', 'If you''re struggling with this then it must be very difficult to shoot. Nice result.', '2007-03-07 18:08:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439895, 475716, 20530, '<td valign="top">Nice contrast and cool reflection. I think it''s a great concept and you almost nailed it. The ice cube looks a little muddy and yellowish. The fire is interesting and colorful, but I find myself wishing at least some of it were in focus. Those are the reasons that the subjects don''t hold my attention for very long. <br/> <br/>The large amount of negative space doesn''t do much for me either. A horizontal crop might have been better suited to  this setup; with the ice cube on the intersection of thirds and the fire along the lower third line. <br/> <br/>I''m envious of your granite. It''s sure to provide you with many great opportunities for reflection shots. Don''t be discouraged. My photos never score as high as I expect them to, either:)</td>', 'Nice contrast and cool reflection. I think it''s a great concept and you almost nailed it. The ice cube looks a little muddy and yellowish. The fire is interesting and colorful, but I find myself wishing at least some of it were in focus. Those are the reasons that the subjects don''t hold my attention for very long.  The large amount of negative space doesn''t do much for me either. A horizontal crop might have been better suited to  this setup; with the ice cube on the intersection of thirds and the fire along the lower third line.  I''m envious of your granite. It''s sure to provide you with many great opportunities for reflection shots. Don''t be discouraged. My photos never score as high as I expect them to, either:)', '2007-03-07 18:30:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440002, 475716, 73121, '<td valign="top">I agree with the others comments about the reflection, I like it.  One thing I may have done differntly is to have bigger flames in the back with *maybe* one or two more cubes out front.<br/> <br/>Though, I am not sure I would be brave enough to have a much larger open flame in my house :)</td>', 'I agree with the others comments about the reflection, I like it.  One thing I may have done differntly is to have bigger flames in the back with *maybe* one or two more cubes out front. Though, I am not sure I would be brave enough to have a much larger open flame in my house :)', '2007-03-07 18:50:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440056, 475053, 52521, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments. I wish I could have applied different curves for the foreground and the background, but as this was s basic-editing challenge this was not allowed ;)</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments. I wish I could have applied different curves for the foreground and the background, but as this was s basic-editing challenge this was not allowed ;)', '2007-03-07 19:03:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440064, 474234, 26733, '<td valign="top">Very cool! Congratulations.</td>', 'Very cool! Congratulations.', '2007-03-07 19:05:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440069, 476656, 26733, '<td valign="top">Beautiful! The outtake is great too.</td>', 'Beautiful! The outtake is great too.', '2007-03-07 19:06:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440119, 476589, 55838, '<td valign="top">HAHAHA!  How cute!  I didn''t vote in this challenge so I''m seeing this for the first time.  That''s not a self portrait is it??  : )  I know I''ve felt kind of like that this week!</td>', 'HAHAHA!  How cute!  I didn''t vote in this challenge so I''m seeing this for the first time.  That''s not a self portrait is it??  : )  I know I''ve felt kind of like that this week!', '2007-03-07 19:16:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440152, 476500, 55838, '<td valign="top">Very pretty Jude and a good idea too.  I really like the reflections and the soft pink tones.  The composition and perspective are well done.  Don''t forget - I think you can clone out sensor dust in basic editing rules now - not that it''s really significant in your shot.  Rockin'' score sister!!  And look at your score from commenters and no camera!  No cameras are often hard to please.  Congratulations!  Very creative &amp; well done!</td>', 'Very pretty Jude and a good idea too.  I really like the reflections and the soft pink tones.  The composition and perspective are well done.  Don''t forget - I think you can clone out sensor dust in basic editing rules now - not that it''s really significant in your shot.  Rockin'' score sister!!  And look at your score from commenters and no camera!  No cameras are often hard to please.  Congratulations!  Very creative & well done!', '2007-03-07 19:22:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440158, 476520, 52521, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju Bragi, ég hafði eitt sæti af þér með 0.0010 stigum, missti af þessari í kosningunni (náði ekki að klára). Hefðir eflaust haft þessi 0.0010 stig ef ég hefði klárað :D</td>', 'Til hamingju Bragi, ég hafði eitt sæti af þér með 0.0010 stigum, missti af þessari í kosningunni (náði ekki að klára). Hefðir eflaust haft þessi 0.0010 stig ef ég hefði klárað :D', '2007-03-07 19:23:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440389, 476829, 19178, '<td valign="top">nICE shot!</td>', 'nICE shot!', '2007-03-07 19:57:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440401, 474278, 42567, '<td valign="top">So cool!  Thanks for the setup pictures!  Congratulations on the top 20</td>', 'So cool!  Thanks for the setup pictures!  Congratulations on the top 20', '2007-03-07 19:59:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440456, 475983, 47906, '<td valign="top">The only major thin I would have done differently on this shot was to align the water so it flows out of the left of the frame and crop out the upper part of the frame so the bend in the river does not show. This would make a powerful diagonal in your shot give allot of depth to the photo.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps,<br/>Rich</td>', 'The only major thin I would have done differently on this shot was to align the water so it flows out of the left of the frame and crop out the upper part of the frame so the bend in the river does not show. This would make a powerful diagonal in your shot give allot of depth to the photo. Hope this helps,Rich', '2007-03-07 20:13:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3440576, 475227, 5792, '<td valign="top">Positives:<br/>Interesting perspective showing the icicles but not their base attachment. Though small it is nice you capture a drop falling. Composition works well.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>Icicle soft focus is this image''s greatest defect. The entire composition is directed to them so they should be as technically perfect as possible. Overall composition is weak.<br/> <br/>Lighting is OK but not exceptional. Early morning and late afternoon are the best times for outdoor phototography because that is when there is the most interesting lighting and shadow. The icicle composition would benefit from that type of lighting. Background softness and content is OK but not very interesting.<br/> <br/>The blue spot in the BG just below one of the icicles competes with it for attention so therefore acts as a distraction.<br/> <br/>Looks like the image is not ''level'' and tilted several degrees off vertical, a problem I have a lot myself. :) If done intentionally then I''d recommend at least a 15 degree angle. The human eye normally wants things at lesser angles to be perfectly vertical.<br/> <br/>The challenge:<br/>Obviously this fits the challenge. There is a long tradition of icicles imagery at DPC. The highest scoring ones are techically perfect images most often with one of more drops of water as prominent elements of the composition. You may want to review some of those for yourself to see what makes them ''good''.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-07 20:58:45.</i></td>', 'Positives:Interesting perspective showing the icicles but not their base attachment. Though small it is nice you capture a drop falling. Composition works well. Technicals:Icicle soft focus is this image''s greatest defect. The entire composition is directed to them so they should be as technically perfect as possible. Overall composition is weak. Lighting is OK but not exceptional. Early morning and late afternoon are the best times for outdoor phototography because that is when there is the most interesting lighting and shadow. The icicle composition would benefit from that type of lighting. Background softness and content is OK but not very interesting. The blue spot in the BG just below one of the icicles competes with it for attention so therefore acts as a distraction. Looks like the image is not ''level'' and tilted several degrees off vertical, a problem I have a lot myself. :) If done intentionally then I''d recommend at least a 15 degree angle. The human eye normally wants things at lesser angles to be perfectly vertical. The challenge:Obviously this fits the challenge. There is a long tradition of icicles imagery at DPC. The highest scoring ones are techically perfect images most often with one of more drops of water as prominent elements of the composition. You may want to review some of those for yourself to see what makes them ''good''.', '2007-03-07 20:54:50.000000', '2007-03-07 20:58:45.000000', 0),
