(3455655, 475404, 47906, '<td valign="top">I was one of the people who rated this shot an 8. I liked the simple effectiveness and sheer beauty overall of the photo. I thought you did a great job conveying the challenge topic, and the composition was very good.<br/> <br/>My only thought when I looked at it in voting origionally was that I wished the greens of the stem were a bit darker. I think this would make them pop more and catch the eye better. <br/> <br/>Another thing that has nothing to do with my vote, as I understand that people have to work with what objects they have but to make this stronger, IMO, it would help if the leaves of the stem were a bit closer to the rose.<br/> <br/>Hope this Helps.<br/>Rich</td>', 'I was one of the people who rated this shot an 8. I liked the simple effectiveness and sheer beauty overall of the photo. I thought you did a great job conveying the challenge topic, and the composition was very good. My only thought when I looked at it in voting origionally was that I wished the greens of the stem were a bit darker. I think this would make them pop more and catch the eye better.  Another thing that has nothing to do with my vote, as I understand that people have to work with what objects they have but to make this stronger, IMO, it would help if the leaves of the stem were a bit closer to the rose. Hope this Helps.Rich', '2007-03-13 06:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3455783, 474234, 54885, '<td valign="top">Very good shot!! I love the angle and the lighting and clarity is excellent</td>', 'Very good shot!! I love the angle and the lighting and clarity is excellent', '2007-03-13 08:44:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3456886, 473947, 1024, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting photo, reflections that becom the main subject of the photograph. I love the building and the tree reflections, but the sign is a little distracting.  The puddles edge, where the snow is, is a very nice touch, it gives some sense of reality to an otherwise "fantasy" photo.  <br/> <br/>The colors do seem a little flat and the photo could use a little more zing.  If this was my photo, I would play with the contract and the color balance just a little bit to add the missing ingredient.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a very good photograph, but it lacks punch and that gives it too much of a snapshot feel.  Very good try, I suggest you might wantto play with this idea a bit more.  I look for a future Monet from you.</td>', 'This is an interesting photo, reflections that becom the main subject of the photograph. I love the building and the tree reflections, but the sign is a little distracting.  The puddles edge, where the snow is, is a very nice touch, it gives some sense of reality to an otherwise "fantasy" photo.   The colors do seem a little flat and the photo could use a little more zing.  If this was my photo, I would play with the contract and the color balance just a little bit to add the missing ingredient. Overall this is a very good photograph, but it lacks punch and that gives it too much of a snapshot feel.  Very good try, I suggest you might wantto play with this idea a bit more.  I look for a future Monet from you.', '2007-03-13 15:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3456948, 476364, 1024, '<td valign="top">Comment: <br/>Hi, Greetings from the Critique Club: <br/> <br/>Composition: The composition of this photo is one of its strongest points.  The shoreline is a very strong diagional leading line and it leads the eye direstly to the main subject.  The red lighthouse is an awesome subject, vibrant where the rest of the photo has a very somber feel to it.<br/> <br/>Technical: The technical post processing is very well done.  You have managed to bring out the darkness of the sky, the brightness of the lighthouse, but still kept the whiteness of the snow.  You might have sacrificed a little of the detail in the snow though, it does seems a little bit washed out.<br/> <br/>Overall: I feel you were on the right track...and you knew what you wanted.  Overall this is a powerful image and one you should be proud of. Good luck and happy shooting.</td>', 'Comment: Hi, Greetings from the Critique Club:  Composition: The composition of this photo is one of its strongest points.  The shoreline is a very strong diagional leading line and it leads the eye direstly to the main subject.  The red lighthouse is an awesome subject, vibrant where the rest of the photo has a very somber feel to it. Technical: The technical post processing is very well done.  You have managed to bring out the darkness of the sky, the brightness of the lighthouse, but still kept the whiteness of the snow.  You might have sacrificed a little of the detail in the snow though, it does seems a little bit washed out. Overall: I feel you were on the right track...and you knew what you wanted.  Overall this is a powerful image and one you should be proud of. Good luck and happy shooting.', '2007-03-13 16:32:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3457023, 476585, 1024, '<td valign="top">Comment: <br/>Hi, Greetings from the Critique Club: <br/> <br/>Composition: Very strong composition, maybe because it is so simple.  The few lines, bend of her wrist, shape of her stomach, all lead the eye directly to the subject ice cube.  <br/> <br/>Technical: The lighting is perfect on this image, from the light directly on her fingers, to the light on her stomach, to the light that seems to be coming from inside the ice cube..  Very well done.  The color temperature give it a very sensual feeling that compliments the subject very well.<br/> <br/>Overall: I think you captured the image exactly how you saw it in your minds eye.  This is an image you should be very proud of.</td>', 'Comment: Hi, Greetings from the Critique Club:  Composition: Very strong composition, maybe because it is so simple.  The few lines, bend of her wrist, shape of her stomach, all lead the eye directly to the subject ice cube.   Technical: The lighting is perfect on this image, from the light directly on her fingers, to the light on her stomach, to the light that seems to be coming from inside the ice cube..  Very well done.  The color temperature give it a very sensual feeling that compliments the subject very well. Overall: I think you captured the image exactly how you saw it in your minds eye.  This is an image you should be very proud of.', '2007-03-13 17:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459124, 476065, 70828, '<td valign="top">WILSONNNNNNNNNNN!  :)</td>', 'WILSONNNNNNNNNNN!  :)', '2007-03-14 07:27:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3460627, 476065, 40973, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! <img alt="'' . substr(''//blackyak.com/dpc/sucker.gif'', strrpos(''//blackyak.com/dpc/sucker.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//blackyak.com/dpc/sucker.gif"/> <br/> <br/>The Butterflies of the Suck League are proud to announce the award of the OOBIE sucker for "Time-out". The OOBIE, "Out Of the Box", is for photos that meet the challenge in a creative fashion that DPC voters might not have properly appreciated.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=562688" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Announcement</a> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Congratulations!   The Butterflies of the Suck League are proud to announce the award of the OOBIE sucker for "Time-out". The OOBIE, "Out Of the Box", is for photos that meet the challenge in a creative fashion that DPC voters might not have properly appreciated. Announcement  ', '2007-03-14 12:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3460967, 476829, 5792, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nshapiro:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=476829" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/640/thumb/476829.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/640/thumb/476829.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/640/thumb/476829.jpg"/></a></i></td></tr></table> <br/>Positives:<br/>Great choice of blue tones. General overall technical quality is good. Tonality is nice.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>The image contains a few white specks that should be cloned out. Unsure but think that would be allowed in basic editing now. It is slightly oversharpened, but not much. The interior of the ''porpoise'' has some oversharpened spots. Lighting is OK.<br/> <br/>The challenge:<br/>Meets the challenge. That is no problem. Your assumption that voters would see the ''porpoise'' and vote it higher as a result is probably in error and explains why it scored lower than you thought.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>Clone out the white specks. The brightest areas of the interior of the ''porpoise'' should be toned down. Unsure if this is possible in basic but reducing overall sharpness would help with this. Overall composition is not bad, but you might want to experiment with other framing to see if it ''looks better''.</td>', 'Originally posted by nshapiro:  Positives:Great choice of blue tones. General overall technical quality is good. Tonality is nice. Technicals:The image contains a few white specks that should be cloned out. Unsure but think that would be allowed in basic editing now. It is slightly oversharpened, but not much. The interior of the ''porpoise'' has some oversharpened spots. Lighting is OK. The challenge:Meets the challenge. That is no problem. Your assumption that voters would see the ''porpoise'' and vote it higher as a result is probably in error and explains why it scored lower than you thought. Suggestions:Clone out the white specks. The brightest areas of the interior of the ''porpoise'' should be toned down. Unsure if this is possible in basic but reducing overall sharpness would help with this. Overall composition is not bad, but you might want to experiment with other framing to see if it ''looks better''.', '2007-03-14 13:44:45.000000', NULL, 0),
